---
/**
 * The name, as the site sets it everywhere it appears: "Oh Hi" as ink on the
 * theme's own ==highlight== pair, then "markdown" with the voice dropped
 * (regular weight, muted ink) and its "mark" leaning in Public Sans's real
 * 400 italic, never a synthesised one. It takes the size of the line it
 * sits in — the header link, a heading, the lede — so one component serves
 * them all; the rules are `.wordmark` in styles/site.css. Chris's wife,
 * 2026-10-16: the highlighter and the lean belong wherever the name is set,
 * the headings included.
 */
---
<span class="wordmark"><span class="hi">Oh Hi</span> <span class="md"><em>mark</em>down</span></span>
